WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.879
In Python, a for loop is used to iterate over a

00:00:04.879 --> 00:00:09.758
sequence of items. We'll use range(3) to see how it works.

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:15.598
range(3) generates numbers 0, 1, and 2. In a for loop,

00:00:15.598 --> 00:00:21.047
it will iterate over these numbers, allowing us to perform actions

00:00:21.047 --> 00:00:22.533
for each number.

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:28.475
Here's how we use range(3) in a for loop. The loop

00:00:28.475 --> 00:00:33.543
will execute three times, once for each number in range(3).

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:39.934
Let's see a simple example. We'll print each number in range(3).

00:00:39.934 --> 00:00:45.968
This loop will run three times, printing 0, 1, and 2.
